Subject: [PATCH] Preserve distinct file list names with equal locale collation

Windows locale collation can equate different Unicode characters, such as
U+002E FULL STOP and U+2024 ONE DOT LEADER. Using that ordering alone in the
file and directory sets rejects valid file lists as containing duplicates.

Keep locale ordering, but break ties by comparing the original UTF-8 names.
Identical names still compare equal and retain the existing duplicate checks.

Applies to the standard DC++ 0.884 source tree.

diff --git a/dcpp/DirectoryListing.h b/dcpp/DirectoryListing.h
--- a/dcpp/DirectoryListing.h
+++ b/dcpp/DirectoryListing.h
@@ -73,7 +73,13 @@
 		typedef unordered_set<TTHValue> TTHSet;
 
 		template<typename T> struct Less {
-			bool operator()(typename T::Ptr a, typename T::Ptr b) const { return compare(a->getName(), b->getName()) < 0; }
+			bool operator()(typename T::Ptr a, typename T::Ptr b) const {
+				const auto& left = a->getName();
+				const auto& right = b->getName();
+				const auto order = compare(left, right);
+				// Locale-equivalent names are not necessarily identical.
+				return order != 0 ? order < 0 : left.compare(right) < 0;
+			}
 		};
 
 		set<Ptr, Less<Directory>> directories;
